[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopStockEntry.cs" id="2_entry"]

; Coyle Ferrin at the Longshore Locker (Phase 38O) — the second fence, and the careless one.
;
; TWO FENCES, NOT ONE, and the pair is the sub-phase's only real content decision. A single fence makes
; contraband a door: you either walk through it or you do not. Two make it a choice, and the two
; differ in the three numbers that matter — what they will take, what they pay, and what the sale
; costs you in standing.
;
; Coyle takes bulk (pelts, cloth, fuel, metal) as well as contraband and pays less for it; Sedge takes
; only the small dear things and pays more. Their standing is mirrored: Coyle is loud, so his sales
; cost -4 with the villagers and earn only +3 with the outlaws, where Sedge's are +5 and -2. Selling
; through Coyle is the fast, expensive road to the same place.
;
; ⚠️ FactionId EMPTY, for the reason spelled out in HollowreachHull.tres: an outlaw-factioned vendor
; starts hostile and is hidden from turn one.
;
; ALWAYS OPEN (OpenHour == CloseHour == 0), against Sedge's 20..5. The wharf must have one counter
; standing at any hour or contraband becomes unsellable for a third of the day, which is a refusal the
; player would read as the mechanic being broken rather than as somebody's opening times.
;
; He is the only seller of the forged writ, which nothing drops — the one contraband good the player
; can only ever buy. It exists to be carried past a warden, which is the loop 38M's gate was built for.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Stock_writ"]
script = ExtResource("2_entry")
ItemId = "item.tome.forged_writ"
Quantity = 2

